    "side": [
      {
        "t": "lead",
        "text": "Litfulo has a boxed warning for serious infections, death, cancer, major heart events and blood clots. Common side effects include headache, diarrhea, acne, rash and hives."
      },
      {
        "t": "list",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "higher risk of serious infections, including tuberculosis, that can lead to hospitalization or death. Malignancies have been reported in people taking Litfulo. Another JAK inhibitor had higher rates of death, lymphoma, lung cancer and major heart events than TNF blockers in rheumatoid arthritis. Blood clots have occurred.",
            "src": [
              {
                "url": "https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=6b2f9446-fb23-4741-b73a-5a2f993733c3",
                "label": "Litfulo label, DailyMed",
                "date": "published Jun 2026"
              }
            ],
            "lead": "Boxed warning:"
          },
          {
            "text": "the most frequent were appendicitis, COVID-19 (including pneumonia) and sepsis. Shingles affecting several skin areas was reported.",
            "src": [
              {
                "url": "https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=6b2f9446-fb23-4741-b73a-5a2f993733c3",
                "label": "Litfulo label, DailyMed",
                "date": "published Jun 2026"
              }
            ],
            "lead": "Serious infections seen:"
          },
          {
            "text": "headache, diarrhea, acne, rash, hives, folliculitis, fever, eczema, dizziness, raised creatine kinase, shingles, lower red blood cell count and mouth sores.",
            "src": [
              {
                "url": "https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=6b2f9446-fb23-4741-b73a-5a2f993733c3",
